00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.910 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  to this festive evening on the occasion  of the start of the czech presidency to  the eu  i would like to invite to the stage  prime minister of the czech republic mr  petrov  please welcome president of the european  commission madame ursula fonder lion  [Applause]  of the european union and the national  anthem of the czech republic  do  [Applause]  so  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  foreign  okay  madam president the floor is yours  thank you very much prime minister via  diapeter ladies and gentlemen  thank you for hosting us in this  stunning castle  which is such an amazing musical program  i know and i learned that smetana was  born here in this castle  but i know also that one of the most  famous czech writers of all times  used to live and teach here in lito  michel  the great always rasik  with his novels  he's shown a light on the long history  of the czech people  from the founders of the nation  to the many unsung heroes who marked  with their courage  the history of your country  since here razak's death almost a  century ago  czechia has continued to inspire the  rest of europe  with the stories  of courage  and bravery  i'm talking of course about the heroes  of 1968  and 1989  i am talking of course about watsonville  who was a leader  and a moral inspiration not only for  czechia but for all europeans  but i'm also talking about the czech  heroes of today  czech families have opened their hearts  and their homes  to ukrainian refugees  czech students have volunteered as  babysitters  for ukrainian children in czech cities  tens of thousands of czech people took  to the streets of prague  to protest against the war and to show  solidarity  with ukraine  once again  the czech people are leading by example  in times of hardship  and adversity  for the next six months the czech  republic will lead the european union as  the presidency of the council  a country that unites north and south  east and west  a country that sits at the very center  of europe  geographically  and culturally  a country that has always been at the  center of european history  and i look forward to working very  closely with you dear peter  in the coming six months  because the tasks that await us are  nothing less than historic  we shall support ukraine in their fight  for freedom and help them overcome this  war  we will break free from our dependency  on russian fossil fuels  we will gain independence and security  of energy supply  through more clean and renewable energy  homegrown  creating jobs here in czechia  we will digitize our economy  and make it more resilient  we will strengthen our democracies  and we will protect our people  all of europe  counts on the czech leadership  in the council on all of these vital  issues in the month ahead of us  the tasks may seem daunting  but in challenging times like these  i always remember a sentence by vatslav  havel  which has accompanied me since the very  early days of my own mandate as  president of the european commission  havel used to say  work  work for something because it is good  not just because it stands a chance to  succeed  end of quote  this is what must drive us  the unity of purpose  the strength of our european values  and the passion for freedom that has  inspired  generations of czech heroes  europe's greatest achievements have  always come when we dared to be bold  and i am glad  that in times like these  europe can count on you  the czech republic  and its amazing people  and now  i'm very much looking forward to hear  the amazing music  of smetana thank you very much  [Applause]  okay  you

